WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.854 --> 00:00:18.355
you hear the big news?"

2
00:00:18.815 --> 00:00:23.218
Flo asked Ally as they were refilling the salt and pepper shakers the next morning at the diner.

3
00:00:23.879 --> 00:00:24.499
Ally gulped.

4
00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:27.961
"Flo likes Ray," she thought.

5
00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:31.144
"So she must be talking about Ray's wife coming back.

6
00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:33.173
I'll just pretend I don't know."

7
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:35.054
"Big news?"

8
00:00:35.515 --> 00:00:36.195
Ally repeated.

9
00:00:36.215 --> 00:00:37.236
"What is it?"

10
00:00:38.256 --> 00:00:39.237
"It's huge!"

11
00:00:39.637 --> 00:00:40.198
Flo said.

12
00:00:40.218 --> 00:00:46.882
"Local bird-watchers spotted a pair of Southwestern bearded whoopers in the desert."

13
00:00:48.964 --> 00:00:49.904
"Oh, that!"

14
00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:51.486
Ally was relieved.

15
00:00:51.506 --> 00:00:54.227
"Yes, I saw that in the newspaper.

16
00:00:55.128 --> 00:00:56.669
The whoopers are endangered, right?

17
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.371
That's why everyone is so excited about them?"

18
00:01:00.151 --> 00:01:04.866
"Yes! People also love them because they have a unique way of flying.

19
00:01:04.886 --> 00:01:07.167
Here, I'll show you a video."

20
00:01:07.527 --> 00:01:12.009
Flo found a video of whoopers flying on her phone and handed the device to Ally.

21
00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:14.089
"Wow!" Ally said.

22
00:01:14.109 --> 00:01:17.111
"It looks like their wings are moving in circles."

23
00:01:19.052 --> 00:01:23.714
While Ally was watching the video, Phil sat down on a stool at the counter next to another

24
00:01:23.754 --> 00:01:26.055
customer. "What are you watching, Ally?"

25
00:01:26.515 --> 00:01:26.975
he asked.

26
00:01:27.975 --> 00:01:29.296
Ally showed Phil the video.

27
00:01:30.112 --> 00:01:32.073
"It looks like they're dancing," Phil said.

28
00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:34.035
"You're right, it does!"

29
00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.796
Ally handed back Flo's phone.

30
00:01:36.816 --> 00:01:39.238
"What can I get for you this morning, Phil?"

31
00:01:39.258 --> 00:01:43.080
"Two scrambled eggs and toast," Phil replied.

32
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.422
"Eggs and toast, coming up!"

33
00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:50.925
Ally pocketed her order pad and then spread her arms out wide and started spinning them in circles.

34
00:01:51.906 --> 00:01:54.267
"Hey, look at me, I'm a whooper!"

35
00:01:55.984 --> 00:01:57.806
Ally laughed as she headed for the kitchen.

36
00:01:58.166 --> 00:02:02.870
But she was so busy "flying," she didn't notice Randy coming out of the kitchen with a tray

37
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.451
of freshly baked cupcakes.

38
00:02:04.932 --> 00:02:08.435
Ally's spinning "bird" arms hit the tray and sent it flying.

39
00:02:09.035 --> 00:02:11.377
Ally was about to activate her levitating powers.

40
00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:15.721
But the tray seemed to hover in the air for a split second before the customer next to

41
00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:16.762
Phil grabbed it.

42
00:02:17.042 --> 00:02:19.004
The customer set it down on the counter.

43
00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:21.185
Ally blinked in surprise.

44
00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:23.127
"Was I just seeing things?"

45
00:02:23.587 --> 00:02:23.988
she thought.

46
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.881
"Or did that tray freeze in midair?"

47
00:02:28.241 --> 00:02:29.401
She turned to the customer.

48
00:02:34.423 --> 00:02:36.103
you so much for catching the tray!"

49
00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:39.764
"Happy to help," the customer replied.

50
00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:44.465
"Those cupcakes look too delicious to let them get ruined."

51
00:02:44.485 --> 00:02:47.386
"Would you like one?"

52
00:02:47.786 --> 00:02:48.346
Ally asked.

53
00:02:48.366 --> 00:02:50.287
"On the house, of course."

54
00:02:51.487 --> 00:02:53.768
"No, thank you," the customer said.

55
00:02:54.348 --> 00:02:57.990
"But I would love to know where you got your necklace."

56
00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.591
"My necklace?"

57
00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:02.211
Ally looked down.

58
00:03:03.192 --> 00:03:04.472
"Uh-oh!" she thought.

59
00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.854
Her meld medallion had slipped out from under her T-shirt.

60
00:03:08.694 --> 00:03:10.075
Ally quickly tucked it away.

61
00:03:10.095 --> 00:03:13.056
"It's nothing, just a present from my parents.

62
00:03:13.076 --> 00:03:13.556
More coffee?"

63
00:03:13.576 --> 00:03:22.460
"It's such an unusual piece—you must have very interesting parents," the customer said.

64
00:03:23.344 --> 00:03:25.106
"Are they world travelers?"

65
00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.569
"Um Ally smiled.

66
00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:29.970
"You could say that."

67
00:03:31.112 --> 00:03:35.596
The customer smiled back and laid a fifty-dollar bill on the counter to pay for her food.

68
00:03:37.878 --> 00:03:41.041
Ally started to give her change when the customer waved her off.

69
00:03:41.061 --> 00:03:43.683
"Keep it," she said with a smile.

70
00:03:43.703 --> 00:03:47.026
"And watch out for falling trays of cupcakes!"

71
00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:56.278
"She was so nice, and generous too," Ally thought as the customer left the diner.

72
00:03:56.298 --> 00:03:59.800
"Silly me, I imagined that tray floating in the air!"

73
00:04:05.322 --> 00:04:08.503
That afternoon Mateo came into the diner with a tall woman.

74
00:04:09.584 --> 00:04:12.145
She was wearing a beautiful dress and high heels.

75
00:04:13.325 --> 00:04:15.526
She looked like someone out of a fashion magazine.

76
00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.668
"Ally, this is my mother, Dawn," Mateo said.

77
00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:23.470
"It's so nice to meet you, Ally," Dawn said.

78
00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.851
"Mateo has told me so much about you."

79
00:04:27.372 --> 00:04:29.753
"I hope he hasn't said too much!"

80
00:04:30.174 --> 00:04:31.394
Ally laughed nervously.

81
00:04:31.414 --> 00:04:33.095
"Where's Ray?"

82
00:04:33.115 --> 00:04:36.137
"He had an errand to run," Dawn said.

83
00:04:36.157 --> 00:04:40.480
"I was so excited for my mom to see the diner, we came straight here."

84
00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:47.504
Mateo gave Dawn a quick tour, pointing out all the changes in the decor and showing her the

85
00:04:47.544 --> 00:04:48.024
new menu.

86
00:04:50.892 --> 00:04:52.874
"And here's Gourmet Greta's review."

87
00:04:53.594 --> 00:04:56.777
Ally pointed out the framed copy of the review hanging on the wall.

88
00:04:56.797 --> 00:04:59.439
"Greta loves it here!"

89
00:04:59.459 --> 00:05:01.521
"That's nice."

90
00:05:02.261 --> 00:05:05.924
Dawn smiled, but Ally could see she was thinking about something else.

91
00:05:06.845 --> 00:05:13.090
After a quick scan of Dawn's thoughts, Ally realized Mateo's mom was thinking about the fancy city restaurants

92
00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.071
she'd gotten used to.

93
00:05:15.572 --> 00:05:17.374
Ray's Diner was nothing like them.

94
00:05:18.295 --> 00:05:20.276
Dawn turned back to Ally.

95
00:05:20.296 --> 00:05:23.838
"I'm happy my sewing room is being put to good use as a place for you to stay.

96
00:05:23.858 --> 00:05:26.099
For now, anyway."

97
00:05:26.119 --> 00:05:28.581
"'For now'?"

98
00:05:29.121 --> 00:05:29.661
Ally thought.

99
00:05:30.242 --> 00:05:33.344
She spun around so no one could see her worried expression.

100
00:05:33.364 --> 00:05:37.306
"Yikes, Dawn does want her sewing room back.

101
00:05:37.886 --> 00:05:40.728
I really hope I can get onboard that P.O.D.!"
